# The settings of codetwine-loom. Put it as .env in the directory the command is run from (cp codetwine_loom/.env.example .env).
# A name the shell sets to a value wins, and one it leaves empty is filled from here. Every setting is listed in docs/settings.md

# The API key, of the provider litellm picks by the model name's prefix
LLM_API_KEY=

# The parent model of the stages that do not decide what is done, such as the editing agent (litellm form). It also writes the design documents --doc-create makes, unless DOC_CREATE_MODEL is set
# MEDIUM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5

# The parent model of the stages that decide what is done: the planning, splitting and merging stages (litellm form)
# HIGH_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5-5

# An endpoint other than the provider's own, such as Ollama
# LLM_API_BASE=

# The proxy the model's API and the web APIs are reached through, as an http:// or https:// URL (the user and the password in ASCII, a '#', '/', '?', '[', ']' or '\' in them written %23, %2F, %3F, %5B, %5D, %5C). HTTP_PROXY / ALL_PROXY and the same names in lower case are read too
# The container that fetches dependencies is given the proxy variables and SSL_CERT_FILE. The container a change is made in is given neither
# HTTPS_PROXY=

# The hosts reached without the proxy, separated by commas, each a host alone with no scheme or port, and without a leading '.' where it names the endpoint's host itself (localhost, the host of LLM_API_BASE inside the network)
# NO_PROXY=

# A PEM file of the certificate authorities to trust in place of the default ones, for a proxy that signs TLS with its own
# SSL_CERT_FILE=

# low / medium / high. The column of settings that raise and lower accuracy together with cost and time. Not the model's effort (that is THINK_LEVEL)
# PRESET=medium

# In a run made in a container, how many times one agent may download from the internet the packages a change adds. 0, they are not downloaded
# The dependencies the repository already has are downloaded. A change that adds a dependency may not pass its tests
#? n=0 Download the packages a change adds, in container runs?
# WARM_MAX_REFILL=3

# Where web_search searches. Empty, web_search is not used
#   model  = the model provider's own search, with the LLM key. Works with Anthropic / OpenAI / Gemini. The provider charges for each search
#   tavily / brave / ollama = that search API. Its key goes in WEB_SEARCH_API_KEY
# WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER=

# The key of the search API named above
# WEB_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# Where web_fetch reads a page through. Empty, web_fetch is not used. It reads only the URLs web_search returned, so it needs WEB_SEARCH_* as well
#   tavily / ollama / jina = that page-reading API. Its key goes in WEB_FETCH_API_KEY; with the same name in WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER, WEB_SEARCH_API_KEY is used
# WEB_FETCH_PROVIDER=

# The key of the page-reading API named above
# WEB_FETCH_API_KEY=

# The target repository. --project gives it too
# PROJECT_DIR=

# Where the target repository's tests live, relative to its root. Empty, the primary language's default (tests / src/test/java / src/test/kotlin / test / tests/testthat), or of it and the language's other test directories (Python test / testing, JavaScript and TypeScript tests, C / C++ and C# test), the one in the repository holding the most source files. A repository with no tests gets its first ones there
# TEST_PATH=

# The model codetwine writes the design documents with, which --doc-create calls (litellm form). Empty, MEDIUM_MODEL
#? skip
# DOC_CREATE_MODEL=

# off / low / medium / high. How much the model thinks while it writes the design documents
#? skip
# DOC_CREATE_EFFORT=low

# Only when the design documents are made (codetwine reads it). Empty, doc_template.json at the top of the repository this tool was installed from
# DOC_TEMPLATE_PATH=/abs/path/to/codetwine-loom/doc_template.json
